  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Vocabulary sources",
      "items": [
        "The bundled list loads with the page, works offline, and is filtered by category. (index.html:7–8, 29–39; README.md:28–30)",
        "Online mode sends the topic to Datamuse, then translates related English terms through MyMemory. Datamuse failure falls back to the topic alone; if translation yields no usable words, the session cannot start. (js/vocabulary-api.js:12–50, 55–83, 86–125)",
        "The online services depend on the network. The topic goes to Datamuse and vocabulary terms go to MyMemory. (README.md:32–34, 60–62)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Practice and progress",
      "items": [
        "Typed and multiple-choice answers update the score and SRS record. Lower past success raises a word's selection weight. (js/answers-and-progress.js:28–45; js/multiple-choice.js:56–75; js/spaced-repetition.js:8–23, 26–47)",
        "Matching displays up to eight pairs and starts another round when all are matched. Its handler does not update answer counts or SRS progress. (js/matching.js:9–20, 51–89)",
        "Progress stays in this browser under germanSRS. Reset removes that key; clearing browser storage also removes the saved record. (js/spaced-repetition.js:1–5; js/answers-and-progress.js:68–79; README.md:60–62)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Hosting and checks",
      "items": [
        "The README links to the hosted GitHub Pages app. The checked-in files don't specify the Pages deployment branch or source setting. (README.md:8–10, 24–30)",
        "The Jekyll Docker workflow runs on pushes and pull requests to main and builds the site; it has no publish step. (README.md:52–58; .github/workflows/jekyll-docker.yml:1–19)",
        "For local use, open index.html directly; no build or package install is required. (README.md:28–30)"
      ]
    }
  ]
